Meta.documentation:cast
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:The content-type → resource casting rules, shared by loading
Meta.documentation:schemes (http:, https:, file: read). The implementation lives on the
Meta.documentation:Dawn runtime as library functions (public/dawn.js, next to require and
Meta.documentation:isBrowser) - this file only documents them; they are not resources.
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:Like the URI philosophy: a loaded thing becomes the right resource
Meta.documentation:for its content - never by the extension or scheme the author
Meta.documentation:guessed beforehand. Dawn.cast(contentType, bytes, url) resolution
Meta.documentation:walks the dawn tree, first hit wins:
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:Content-Type.<type>.<subtype> - a specialized mimetype resource
Meta.documentation:dropped into the tree; Content-Type.<type> - a family main resource
Meta.documentation:(Content-Type/text, Content-Type/image, Content-Type/application/json
Meta.documentation:are seeded); then the built-in defaults: text/* → data.String,
Meta.documentation:image/svg+xml → data.String (markup text), application/json →
Meta.documentation:data.Data, anything else → application.octetstream.
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:The found resource is fed the raw bytes through its octetstream interface
Meta.documentation:(in_octetstream_$all) - every value resource parses its own bytes - and
Meta.documentation:the true content-type is stamped on it, so reply paths prefer it. After
Meta.documentation:casting, the value late-connects to the next resource in the flow
Meta.documentation:so bindings reflect the true type.
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:Dawn.castValue(type, value) is the native-value sibling: it wraps an
Meta.documentation:already-typed JS value (string, BigRational, boolean, object,
Meta.documentation:Uint8Array) in its own resource for late-connect - used by the
Meta.documentation:List operators, whose element types are known only at execution
Meta.documentation:time. Dawn.u8ToBase64/Dawn.base64ToU8 are shared Uint8Array helpers.
Meta.documentation:
Meta.documentation:@kind operator
Meta.documentation:@status internal
